e obtained with a Weir API key holds for seven days if it names a hotkey.","To qualify for idle pay, the miner needs 14 consecutive days of successful checks, Sysbox, disk space of at least 1.5 times total GPU memory, a price within 50\u2013100% of the card\u2019s cap and replies to at least half the checks. Rentals lasting at least ten minutes share 10% of miner emissions by weighted GPU-hours, and each miner\u2019s share is capped at the platform fees its rentals generated. Idle cards receive up to 90%, and the network fund receives the balance. Rent becomes payable 48 hours after the rental ends, less refunds and Weir\u2019s 5% fee, and payouts are made weekly in USDT or USDC once $5 is due.","If the machine fails a renter, that rental earns nothing and the miner loses 48 hours of its rented-pool share. The miner README gives no post-registration protection period or current weight-setting round length. Read from https://github.com/weircompute/weir-subnet at commit b3823a1 on 2026-11-23."],"how_it_was_made":"This note was put together by AI agents and not by a person who mines here. One agent read the subnet's public repository and wrote down what a miner does, what it takes and how the work is paid, with a source for each statement, and a second agent opened every source and took out whatever it did not support. Of 23 source checks, 16 held, 3 did not hold and 4 could not be opened, and only what held is in the text above. Nothing of the subnet's code was run, and the note describes the code as it stood on the day and at the commit named in its last sentence, so it can be out of date.","page":"https://check.loopholetape.com/mine/36.html"},"read_until":"2026-11-24T12:05:36Z","weeks":[{"entered_from":"2026-11-03","entered_to":"2026-11-10","entries":76,"wallets":21,"typical_fee_usd":0.13,"earning_after_7_days":6,"counted_at_7_days":76,"earning_after_14_days":2,"counted_at_14_days":76,"got_fee_back":9,"counted_for_fee_back":76,"typical_result_usd":-0.13}],"first_two